  "notes": "The capture is dominated by a Quick Start modal that opens on load; the app behind it is blurred and dimmed. Closing it (X, Escape or a backdrop click) shows a near-black pro video tool (Electron app run in a browser) with three columns. The center shows seven synced viewer tiles of one clip: Reference, Camera Path (blue camera icon and track points), Pose (2D skeleton overlay), Depth, Edges, Masks, 3D Stick Figure. Each tile is a bordered article with a 32px dark header strip. Electric blue #1688ff marks selection (selected option card border, active layer chips, step dots); cyan #74e8f2 is used for links; green #68ff80 is used for good status (the 'Actor motion' pill, OK quality labels); salmon #ff887a is used for the Cancel button. Most controls in the capture were disabled while analysis was running (the stage chips Prepare, Pose, Camera, Encode, Bundle show pipeline progress). The workflow stepper in the header only displays progress and is not clickable. The Export Presets row uses letter-glyph tiles (S Seedance, C ComfyUI, B Blender, R Runway, K Kling) as multi-select toggles. Proposal filed: modal-dialog purpose 'help-or-instructions'."
